{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-c8:000011:note_appended:sase-c8:796edb7ab60f7ec0567121e7bac644e5c307b3c1ac6a7210026fd88a1a5dcc33","timestamp":"2026-07-31T14:36:27Z","actor":"sase-c8","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"sase-c8","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Replaced the RuntimeError in handle_bead_ref with a real add/rm slow path: it now re-enters the Rust bead CLI core via the new bead_fast_path.execute_bead_cli(..., materialize=True), which resolves and materializes the bead store when the early fast-path context resolution declines (the failure mode that produced 'was not handled by the Rust fast path'). Unknown ref actions now exit 1 instead of raising, a bare 'sase bead ref' no longer depends on list-only namespace attrs, and sase artifact create's bead attachment uses the same materializing entry point. Added CLI coverage: add->list->rm->list round trip through handle_bead_ref, missing-issue error path (exit 1, 'Issue not found'), rust-core-unavailable path (exit 1), and a fast-path test proving execute_bead_cli(materialize=True) succeeds where try_handle_bead_fast_path defers. Verified: just fmt, just lint (all green except the pre-existing is_safe_bead_prefix symvision failure already tracked by sase-c1), tests/main + tests/test_bead + artifact create/e2e + changespec refs (2197 passed), and a live 'sase bead ref add/list/rm' smoke test. The 53 ACE PNG snapshot failures in just test reproduce identically on a clean master checkout and are already tracked by sase-c5/sase-c6."}}
